     output vary run to run even at a fixed seed.)
    a text called 'the matched name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reap matched".
    a text called 'the matched init' is "a boolean called {'the matched name'} is false".
    a text called 'the matched set' is "If reaped is {'the child name'} then, Set {'the matched name'} to true".
    a text called 'the match assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-61" and 'the matched name'.
    a text called 'the decoded name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "reproduced exit".
    a text called 'the decoded line' is "a number called {'the decoded name'} is the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256".
    a text called 'the decoded assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-60" and 'the decoded name' and 'the exit code'.
    a text called 'the quoted phrase word' is 'gen word from' of gen_type_words.
    a text called 'the quoted phrase line' is "a text called 'the reaped' is \"{'the quoted phrase word'}\"".
    a text called 'the quoted phrase assert' is "If 'the reaped' is not \"{'the quoted phrase word'}\" then, Print \"ASSERT PRC-60: expected {'the quoted phrase word'} got {{'the reaped'}}\", Exit 95. Print 'the reaped'".
    a text called 'the waiting value' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a number called 'the waiting expected' is 'the waiting value' as a number.
    a text called 'the waiting line' is "a number called waiting is {'the waiting value'}".
    a text called 'the waiting assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-55" and "waiting" and 'the waiting expected'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the child line', 'the child branch', 'the bare set line', 'the matched init', 'the matched set', 'the match assert', 'the decoded line', 'the decoded assert', 'the quoted phrase line', 'the quoted phrase assert', 'the waiting line', 'the waiting assert'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-87: undocumented precision, not a manual sentence - every
 path-taking statement in this section accepts an empty path and fails
 cleanly through the error flag rather than crashing; the memory-safety
 floor for the whole section, and the first degenerate input a leaf will
 produce by accident. This leaf sticks to the three unbanned, non-policy-
 restricted constructs already registered elsewhere in this file - create
 directory, remove directory, symbolic link - and draws which one gets
 the empty path this call, rather than emitting all three every time,
 since the OTHER two still get their ordinary confined exercise from
 kinds 260/263 in the same campaign. `Mount`/`Unmount` (emit-safe but
 covered by kind 262 already) and `Execute` (locked to the fixed
 true/false allowlist by this surface brief's policy, so an empty path is
 not a value this leaf is allowed to hand it) are left out; `Pivot root`
 stays banned. The ledger's own retained probe,
 docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-87.vox, sweeps all eight
 constructs the manual lists in one hand-verification pass; this leaf
 draws one of the three per call so the corpus varies which construct is
 exercised, rather than repeating a fixed eight-statement shape every
 time it is drawn.)
To 'gen leaf process empty path refusal' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    a number called 'the construct draw' is 'rng below' of 3.
    a text called 'the flag name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a text called 'the flag init' is "a boolean called {'the flag name'} is false".
    a text called 'the handler' is "On error Set {'the flag name'} to true".
    a text called 'the assert line' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-87" and 'the flag name'.
    a text called 'the continued' is "Print \"execution continued\"".
    a text called 'the statement' is "Create a directory called \"\"".
    If 'the construct draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the statement' to "Remove the directory called \"\"".
    If 'the construct draw' is 2 then,
        Set 'the statement' to "Create symbolic link from \"\" to \"\"".
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the flag init', 'the statement', 'the handler', 'the assert line', 'the continued'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(Process leaves, batch C (2026-10-05), kinds 420-427 - the THIRD
 reservation for this surface, docs/ledger/process-control.md rows
 PRC-06 to 10, 14 to 20 and 22 to 24. Same safety posture as batches A
 and B. TheJostler ruled (see also PROCEDURE.md sect.6) that mount,
 unmount and device-node creation are SAFE TO EMIT because the kernel refuses each of them to an
 unprivileged process before it acts - hand-verified this batch with
 strace on the installed 0.4.15: every one lowers to a single plain
 mount(2), umount2(2) or mknod(2) and returns EPERM, so none can wait
 on an interactive authorisation the way `Shutdown` was seen to (none
 of these leaves emits `Shutdown`). Every path lives under the
 program's own scratch directory; the one successful `Change directory`
 runs only inside a forked child, which this leaf reaps, so no sibling
 leaf's scratch-relative path ever moves; and the device-node type is
 only ever "c" or "b" - never "p", which creates a real FIFO with no
 privilege at all (Discrepancy 1), and which tests/200_never_emitted.vox
 now guards against in place of its old blanket device-node needle.)

(The last part of a scratch path in this batch - a place, so a path
 reads as somewhere a directory could stand. Nothing in the manual
 constrains a path component, so the word is drawn; the per-program
 counter appended after it is what keeps two paths from colliding.)
a list called gen_process_place_words is ["harbour", "quay", "jetty", "berth", "wharf", "landing", "dock", "pier", "mooring", "haven", "cove", "inlet", "boathouse", "lock", "weir", "sluice", "staithe", "hithe", "basin", "marina"].

(A run of DISTINCT places for a leaf that names several paths at once:
 a random starting point, then consecutive words, so no two paths in
 the same leaf can draw the same word and declare the same variable
 twice.)
To 'gen process places' with a number called 'how many'.
    a number called 'the word count' is gen_process_place_words's length.
    a number called 'the start' is 'rng below' of 'the word count'.
    a list called 'the places' is [].
    a number called 'the position' is 0.
    While 'the position' is less than 'how many',
        a number called 'the slot' is {'the start' add 'the position'} modulo 'the word count' add 1,
        a text called 'the place' is element 'the slot' of gen_process_place_words,
        append 'the place' to 'the places',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    Return a list, 'the places'.

(Whether a path statement names its path through the variable holding
 it or spells the path again as a format-string literal. The manual
 shows both (LANGUAGE.md:4234-4236 literals, 4241 a `'<path>'`
 variable) and both were hand-verified this batch for directories,
 mount, unmount and device nodes; neither is canonical, so it is drawn.)
To 'gen process path operand' with a text called 'the variable' and a text called 'the literal'.
    a number called 'the spelling draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the spelling draw' is 1 then,
        Return a text, 'the literal'.
    Return a text, 'the variable'.

(The directory creation statement with its optional article drawn
 (LANGUAGE.md:4241-4242), so a leaf that only needs a directory to
 exist does not stamp one spelling of it into every program.)
To 'gen process create directory' with a text called 'the operand'.
    a number called 'the article draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the article draw' is 1 then,
        Return a text, "Create directory called {'the operand'}".
    Return a text, "Create a directory called {'the operand'}".

(rmdir(2) in any of its eight spellings: `Remove` or `Delete`, with or
 without `the`, with or without `called` (LANGUAGE.md:4243-4244) - all
 eight hand-verified this batch to compile and remove the directory.
 The caller draws the three choices (each 0 or 1) so it knows which row
 the spelling puts on trial; 'gen process any removal' draws them here.)
To 'gen process removal statement' with a text called 'the operand' and a number called 'the verb draw' and a number called 'the article draw' and a number called 'the called draw'.
    a text called 'the verb' is "Remove".
    If 'the verb draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the verb' to "Delete".
    a text called 'the article' is "".
    If 'the article draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the article' to "the ".
    a text called 'the called word' is "".
    If 'the called draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the called word' to "called ".
    a text called 'the statement' is "{'the verb'} {'the article'}directory {'the called word'}{'the operand'}".
    Return a text, 'the statement'.

To 'gen process any removal' with a text called 'the operand'.
    a number called 'the verb draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a number called 'the article draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a number called 'the called draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the statement' is 'gen process removal statement' of 'the operand' and 'the verb draw' and 'the article draw' and 'the called draw'.
    Return a text, 'the statement'.

(The row a removal spelling puts on trial: PRC-07 for `Delete`, PRC-08
 when `the` or `called` is left out, PRC-06 for the full `Remove the
 directory called`.)
To 'gen process removal row' with a number called 'the verb draw' and a number called 'the article draw' and a number called 'the called draw'.
    If 'the verb draw' is 1 then,
        Return a text, "PRC-07".
    If 'the article draw' is 0 then,
        Return a text, "PRC-08".
    If 'the called draw' is 0 then,
        Return a text, "PRC-08".
    Return a text, "PRC-06".

(The two path assertions this batch makes, as one renderable line each
 in the shape 'gen assert number' documents: an If that closes itself,
 then a plain Print to take the join's punctuation.)
To 'gen process assert present' with a text called 'the row' and a text called 'the path' and a text called 'the shown'.
    a text called 'the line' is "If {'the path'} is not available then, Print \"ASSERT {'the row'}: expected available got missing\", Exit 95. Print \"{'the shown'}\"".
    Return a text, 'the line'.

To 'gen process assert absent' with a text called 'the row' and a text called 'the path' and a text called 'the shown'.
    a text called 'the line' is "If {'the path'} is available then, Print \"ASSERT {'the row'}: expected missing got available\", Exit 95. Print \"{'the shown'}\"".
    Return a text, 'the line'.

(PRC-06, PRC-07, PRC-08: `Remove the directory called '<path>'.` /
 `Delete the directory "<path>".` perform rmdir(2); `Remove` and
 `Delete` both work and `the` and `called` are each optional
 (LANGUAGE.md:4243-4244). One to four sibling directories are created
 and then removed, forwards or backwards, each removal in its own drawn
 spelling naming its path by variable or by literal, and each asserted
 gone afterwards; the assertion carries the row its spelling puts on
 trial (PRC-07 for `Delete`, PRC-08 when `the` or `called` is left out,
 PRC-06 for the full `Remove the directory called`). No removal may
 fire the shared handler.)
To 'gen leaf process directory removal spellings' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If gen_scratch_flag is empty then,
        Print "PROBE PRC-06: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    a text called 'the flag name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a number called 'the directory count' is 'rng below' of 4 add 1.
    a list called 'the places' is 'gen process places' of 'the directory count'.
    a list called 'the path names' is [].
    a list called 'the path literals' is [].
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a text called 'the flag init' is "a boolean called {'the flag name'} is false".
    append 'the flag init' to 'the lines'.
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the directory count',
        a text called 'the place' is element 'the position' of 'the places',
        a text called 'the path name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "{'the place'}",
        a text called 'the path literal' is "\"{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the place'}{'the path number'}\"",
        a text called 'the path line' is "a text called {'the path name'} is {'the path literal'}",
        a text called 'the create line' is 'gen process create directory' of 'the path name',
        append 'the path name' to 'the path names',
        append 'the path literal' to 'the path literals',
        append 'the path line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the create line' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    a number called 'the order draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    Set 'the position' to 1.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the directory count',
        a number called 'the index' is 'the position',
        If 'the order draw' is 1 then,
            Set 'the index' to 'the directory count' subtract 'the position' add 1.
        a text called 'the path name' is element 'the index' of 'the path names',
        a text called 'the path literal' is element 'the index' of 'the path literals',
        a text called 'the operand' is 'gen process path operand' of 'the path name' and 'the path literal',
        a number called 'the verb draw' is 'rng below' of 2,
        a number called 'the article draw' is 'rng below' of 2,
        a number called 'the called draw' is 'rng below' of 2,
        a text called 'the removal' is 'gen process removal statement' of 'the operand' and 'the verb draw' and 'the article draw' and 'the called draw',
        a text called 'the row' is 'gen process removal row' of 'the verb draw' and 'the article draw' and 'the called draw',
        a text called 'the handler' is "On error Set {'the flag name'} to true",
        a text called 'the gone line' is 'gen process assert absent' of 'the row' and 'the path name' and "removed",
        append 'the removal' to 'the lines',
        append 'the handler' to 'the lines',
        append 'the gone line' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    a text called 'the clean assert' is 'gen assert false' of "PRC-06" and 'the flag name'.
    append 'the clean assert' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-09: removal is rmdir(2), so it is not recursive - a directory that
 still holds anything cannot be removed, and what it holds survives
 (LANGUAGE.md:4243; rmdir(2)'s own semantics, cited rather than stated
 in a sentence). The outer directory holds a chain of zero to three
 nested directories and, at the bottom, possibly a written file - at
 least one of the two, so there is always something in the way. The
 refused removal must fire its handler and leave the deepest child in
 place; then the chain is emptied deepest first, each in its own drawn
 spelling, and only then does the outer removal succeed.)
To 'gen leaf process directory removal is not recursive' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If gen_scratch_flag is empty then,
        Print "PROBE PRC-09: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    a text called 'the outer name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a number called 'the depth' is 'rng below' of 4.
    a boolean called 'the file is inside' is false.
    a number called 'the file draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the file draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the file is inside' to true.
    If 'the depth' is 0 then,
        Set 'the file is inside' to true.
    a number called 'the place count' is 'the depth' add 2.
    a list called 'the places' is 'gen process places' of 'the place count'.
    a text called 'the outer place' is element 1 of 'the places'.
    a text called 'the outer path' is "{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the outer place'}{'the path number'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a text called 'the outer line' is "a text called {'the outer name'} is \"{'the outer path'}\"".
    a text called 'the outer create' is 'gen process create directory' of 'the outer name'.
    append 'the outer line' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the outer create' to 'the lines'.
    a list called 'the chain names' is [].
    a text called 'the deepest path' is 'the outer path'.
    a number called 'the level' is 1.
    While 'the level' is less than or equal to 'the depth',
        a number called 'the slot' is 'the level' add 1,
        a text called 'the place' is element 'the slot' of 'the places',
        Set 'the deepest path' to "{'the deepest path'}/{'the place'}",
        a text called 'the chain name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "{'the place'}",
        a text called 'the chain line' is "a text called {'the chain name'} is \"{'the deepest path'}\"",
        a text called 'the chain create' is 'gen process create directory' of 'the chain name',
        append 'the chain name' to 'the chain names',
        append 'the chain line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the chain create' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the level' to 'the level' add 1.
    a text called 'the deepest name' is 'the outer name'.
    If 'the depth' is greater than 0 then,
        Set 'the deepest name' to element 'the depth' of 'the chain names'.
    a text called 'the file name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "keepsake".
    a text called 'the handle name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "scribe".
    If 'the file is inside' then,
        a number called 'the last slot' is 'the depth' add 2,
        a text called 'the file place' is element 'the last slot' of 'the places',
        Set 'the deepest name' to 'the file name',
        a number called 'the payload length' is 'rng below' of 40 add 1,
        a text called 'the payload' is 'gen buffer filler' of 'the payload length',
        a text called 'the file line' is "a text called {'the file name'} is \"{'the deepest path'}/{'the file place'}\"",
        a text called 'the open line' is "open a file for writing called {'the handle name'} at {'the file name'}",
        a text called 'the write line' is "Write \"{'the payload'}\" to {'the handle name'}",
        a text called 'the close line' is "Close {'the handle name'}",
        append 'the file line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the open line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the write line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the close line' to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the refused' is 'gen buffer companion' of "refused".
    a text called 'the refused init' is "a boolean called {'the refused'} is false".
    a text called 'the outer literal' is "\"{'the outer path'}\"".
    a text called 'the outer operand' is 'gen process path operand' of 'the outer name' and 'the outer literal'.
    a text called 'the refused removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the outer operand'.
    a text called 'the refused handler' is "On error Set {'the refused'} to true".
    a text called 'the refused assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-09" and 'the refused'.
    a text called 'the survivor assert' is 'gen process assert present' of "PRC-09" and 'the deepest name' and "survived".
    append 'the refused init' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the refused removal' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the refused handler' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the refused assert' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the survivor assert' to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the emptying' is 'gen buffer companion' of "emptying failed".
    a text called 'the emptying init' is "a boolean called {'the emptying'} is false".
    a text called 'the emptying handler' is "On error Set {'the emptying'} to true".
    append 'the emptying init' to 'the lines'.
    If 'the file is inside' then,
        a text called 'the delete file' is "Delete the file {'the file name'}",
        append 'the delete file' to 'the lines',
        append 'the emptying handler' to 'the lines'.
    Set 'the level' to 'the depth'.
    While 'the level' is greater than 0,
        a text called 'the chain name' is element 'the level' of 'the chain names',
        a text called 'the chain removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the chain name',
        append 'the chain removal' to 'the lines',
        append 'the emptying handler' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the level' to 'the level' subtract 1.
    a text called 'the final removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the outer operand'.
    a text called 'the emptying assert' is 'gen assert false' of "PRC-09" and 'the emptying'.
    a text called 'the gone assert' is 'gen process assert absent' of "PRC-09" and 'the outer name' and "emptied and removed".
    append 'the final removal' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the emptying handler' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the emptying assert' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the gone assert' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-06: the removal really is rmdir(2) and not a general "remove this
 path" - pointed at a regular FILE it refuses (ENOTDIR, seen under
 strace this batch), fires the handler, and the file is still there
 with every byte the leaf wrote, read back through FIL-01's live `size`
 (LANGUAGE.md:4243; FIL-01 is LANGUAGE.md:3832). A removal that quietly
 fell through to unlink(2) would pass a sloppier leaf and fail this
 one.)
To 'gen leaf process directory removal refuses a file' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
