        Print "PROBE PRC-06: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    a text called 'the file name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a text called 'the place' is 'gen word from' of gen_process_place_words.
    a text called 'the file literal' is "\"{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the place'}{'the path number'}\"".
    a text called 'the file line' is "a text called {'the file name'} is {'the file literal'}".
    a text called 'the handle name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "scribe".
    a number called 'the payload length' is 'rng below' of 64.
    a text called 'the payload' is 'gen buffer filler' of 'the payload length'.
    a text called 'the open line' is "open a file for writing called {'the handle name'} at {'the file name'}".
    a text called 'the write line' is "Write \"{'the payload'}\" to {'the handle name'}".
    a text called 'the close line' is "Close {'the handle name'}".
    a text called 'the refused' is 'gen buffer companion' of "refused".
    a text called 'the refused init' is "a boolean called {'the refused'} is false".
    a text called 'the operand' is 'gen process path operand' of 'the file name' and 'the file literal'.
    a number called 'the verb draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a number called 'the article draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a number called 'the called draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the removal' is 'gen process removal statement' of 'the operand' and 'the verb draw' and 'the article draw' and 'the called draw'.
    a text called 'the row' is 'gen process removal row' of 'the verb draw' and 'the article draw' and 'the called draw'.
    a text called 'the handler' is "On error Set {'the refused'} to true".
    a text called 'the refused assert' is 'gen assert true' of 'the row' and 'the refused'.
    a text called 'the present assert' is 'gen process assert present' of 'the row' and 'the file name' and "the file is still there".
    (The reader's name is built from its stem, not taken from 'gen buffer
     companion', so its possessive takes one apostrophe - `'x reader's
     size` - the way 'gen buffer property' spells a quoted name's.)
    a text called 'the reader stem' is "'{gen_buffer_last_word} reader".
    a text called 'the reader name' is "{'the reader stem'}'".
    a text called 'the reader line' is "open a file for reading called {'the reader name'} at {'the file name'}".
    a text called 'the size access' is 'gen buffer property' of 'the reader stem' and "size".
    a text called 'the size assert' is 'gen assert number is' of 'the row' and 'the size access' and 'the payload length'.
    a text called 'the reader close' is "Close {'the reader name'}".
    a text called 'the cleanup' is "Delete the file {'the file name'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the file line', 'the open line', 'the write line', 'the close line', 'the refused init', 'the removal', 'the handler', 'the refused assert', 'the present assert', 'the reader line', 'the size assert', 'the reader close', 'the cleanup'].
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-10: `Change directory to "<path>".` performs chdir(2), and a later
 RELATIVE path resolves from the new working directory
 (LANGUAGE.md:4237, 4245). A successful chdir would move the cwd out
 from under every scratch path a sibling leaf builds afterwards (they
 are relative), so it happens only inside a forked child, which this
 leaf reaps before it ends: the parent's cwd never moves. The child
 changes into a fresh scratch directory and first checks, by a BARE
 name, for a beacon directory the parent made inside it - so if the
 chdir silently failed the child exits with a stray code before it
 creates anything in the wrong place. Then it creates one to three more
 directories by bare name and exits with a drawn code. The parent
 asserts the child's exit code and finds every bare-named directory at
 the path it has only if the chdir took effect, then clears them all
 away.)
To 'gen leaf process change directory in a child' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If gen_scratch_flag is empty then,
        Print "PROBE PRC-10: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    Set gen_process_has_reaped to true.
    a text called 'the child name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a number called 'the bare count' is 'rng below' of 3 add 1.
    a number called 'the place count' is 'the bare count' add 2.
    a list called 'the places' is 'gen process places' of 'the place count'.
    a text called 'the room place' is element 1 of 'the places'.
    a text called 'the beacon place' is element 2 of 'the places'.
    a text called 'the room path' is "{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the room place'}{'the path number'}".
    a text called 'the room name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "{'the room place'}".
    a text called 'the room line' is "a text called {'the room name'} is \"{'the room path'}\"".
    a text called 'the room create' is 'gen process create directory' of 'the room name'.
    a text called 'the beacon literal' is "\"{'the room path'}/{'the beacon place'}\"".
    a text called 'the beacon create' is 'gen process create directory' of 'the beacon literal'.
    a number called 'the exit code' is 'gen process safe exit code'.
    a number called 'the stray offset' is 'rng below' of 89 add 1.
    a number called 'the stray code' is {'the exit code' add 'the stray offset'} modulo 90.
    a text called 'the room literal' is "\"{'the room path'}\"".
    a text called 'the room operand' is 'gen process path operand' of 'the room name' and 'the room literal'.
    a text called 'the fork line' is "a number called {'the child name'} is fork the process".
    a text called 'the change line' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, Change directory to {'the room operand'}".
    a text called 'the beacon check' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 and \"{'the beacon place'}\" is not available then, Exit {'the stray code'}".
    a text called 'the child actions' is "".
    a number called 'the position' is 3.
    a number called 'the last place' is 'the bare count' add 2.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the last place',
        a text called 'the bare place' is element 'the position' of 'the places',
        a text called 'the bare create' is 'gen process create directory' of "\"{'the bare place'}\"",
        Set 'the child actions' to "{'the child actions'}{'the bare create'}, ",
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    a text called 'the child line' is "If {'the child name'} is 0 then, {'the child actions'}Exit {'the exit code'}".
    a text called 'the reap name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "chdir reaped".
    a text called 'the reap line' is "a number called {'the reap name'} is reap child {'the child name'}".
    a text called 'the exit name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "chdir exit".
    a text called 'the exit line' is "a number called {'the exit name'} is the reaped status divide 256 modulo 256".
    a text called 'the exit assert' is 'gen assert number is' of "PRC-10" and 'the exit name' and 'the exit code'.
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the room line', 'the room create', 'the beacon create', 'the fork line', 'the change line', 'the beacon check', 'the child line', 'the reap line', 'the exit line', 'the exit assert'].
    Set 'the position' to 3.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the last place',
        a text called 'the bare place' is element 'the position' of 'the places',
        a text called 'the composed' is "\"{'the room path'}/{'the bare place'}\"",
        a text called 'the found assert' is 'gen process assert present' of "PRC-10" and 'the composed' and 'the bare place',
        a text called 'the bare removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the composed',
        append 'the found assert' to 'the lines',
        append 'the bare removal' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    a text called 'the beacon removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the beacon literal'.
    a text called 'the room removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the room name'.
    append 'the beacon removal' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the room removal' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(One mount operand in one of the four forms LANGUAGE.md:4262-4264
 allows - a string literal, a text variable, a buffer, or a buffer
 built by a format string - returned as a list: any declaration lines
 first, the operand itself last. The format-built form interpolates a
 text holding 'the stem' and appends 'the suffix', so it spells the same
 value the other forms spell; when 'the stem' is empty (a scratch path,
 which is format-built already) the buffer holds 'the plain' directly.)
To 'gen process mount operand' with a text called 'the name' and a text called 'the plain' and a text called 'the stem' and a text called 'the suffix'.
    a number called 'the form' is 'rng below' of 4.
    a list called 'the parts' is [].
    If 'the form' is 0 then,
        append "\"{'the plain'}\"" to 'the parts',
        Return a list, 'the parts'.
    If 'the form' is 1 then,
        append "a text called {'the name'} is \"{'the plain'}\"" to 'the parts'.
    If 'the form' is 2 then,
        append "a buffer called {'the name'} is \"{'the plain'}\"" to 'the parts'.
    If 'the form' is 3 and 'the stem' is empty then,
        append "a buffer called {'the name'} is \"{'the plain'}\"" to 'the parts'.
    If 'the form' is 3 and 'the stem' is not empty then,
        a text called 'the stem name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "stem",
        append "a text called {'the stem name'} is \"{'the stem'}\"" to 'the parts',
        append "a buffer called {'the name'} is \"{{{'the stem name'}}}{'the suffix'}\"" to 'the parts'.
    append 'the name' to 'the parts'.
    Return a list, 'the parts'.

(Moves a 'gen process mount operand' result's declarations onto the end
 of a leaf's lines and hands back the operand.)
To 'gen process take operand' with a list called 'the parts' and a list called 'the lines'.
    a number called 'the count' is 'the parts's length.
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    While 'the position' is less than 'the count',
        a text called 'the part' is element 'the position' of 'the parts',
        append 'the part' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    a text called 'the operand' is element 'the count' of 'the parts'.
    Return a text, 'the operand'.

(PRC-14: `source`, `target`, `fstype` and `options` each accept a string
 literal, a text variable, or a buffer, including a format-string-built
 buffer (LANGUAGE.md:4262-4264). Each of the four operands draws its own
 form, so every combination appears across a corpus; whether `with
 options` appears at all is drawn too (LANGUAGE.md:4261). The values are
 drawn as well - real filesystem names beside nonsense ones, options a
 kernel would and would not understand, a size from 'gen extreme number'
 - since an unprivileged mount(2) refuses with EPERM before reading any
 of them, which is exactly why every one may be anything. The refusal is
 asserted (the error-flag path is the only one an unprivileged fuzzer
 can reach), then the target is unmounted lazily - also refused - and
 removed.)
To 'gen leaf process mount operand forms' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If gen_scratch_flag is empty then,
        Print "PROBE PRC-14: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    a text called 'the flag name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a text called 'the place' is 'gen word from' of gen_process_place_words.
    a text called 'the target path' is "{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the place'}{'the path number'}".
    a text called 'the directory name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "{'the place'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a text called 'the directory line' is "a text called {'the directory name'} is \"{'the target path'}\"".
    a text called 'the directory create' is 'gen process create directory' of 'the directory name'.
    append 'the directory line' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the directory create' to 'the lines'.
    a list called 'the source words' is ["tmpfs", "ramfs", "proc", "sysfs", "devpts", "mqueue", "cgroup2", "overlay", "nothing at all", "", 'the place'].
    a text called 'the source plain' is 'gen word from' of 'the source words'.
    a text called 'the source name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "source".
    a list called 'the source parts' is 'gen process mount operand' of 'the source name' and 'the source plain' and 'the source plain' and "".
    a text called 'the source operand' is 'gen process take operand' of 'the source parts' and 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the target name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "target".
    a list called 'the target parts' is 'gen process mount operand' of 'the target name' and 'the target path' and "" and "".
    a text called 'the target operand' is 'gen process take operand' of 'the target parts' and 'the lines'.
    a list called 'the type stems' is ["tmp", "ram", "sys", "proc", "hugetlb", "debug", "trace", "config", "squash", "ext4", "x", ""].
    a text called 'the type stem' is 'gen word from' of 'the type stems'.
    a text called 'the type suffix' is "fs".
    If 'the type stem' is "proc" then,
        Set 'the type suffix' to "".
    a text called 'the type plain' is "{'the type stem'}{'the type suffix'}".
    a text called 'the type name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "type".
    a list called 'the type parts' is 'gen process mount operand' of 'the type name' and 'the type plain' and 'the type stem' and 'the type suffix'.
    a text called 'the type operand' is 'gen process take operand' of 'the type parts' and 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the mount line' is "Mount {'the source operand'} at {'the target operand'} with type {'the type operand'}".
    a number called 'the options draw' is 'rng below' of 6.
    If 'the options draw' is greater than 0 then,
        a text called 'the options stem' is "ro",
        a text called 'the options suffix' is "",
        a text called 'the size digits' is 'gen extreme number',
        a text called 'the mode digits' is 'gen random digits' of 3,
        If 'the options draw' is 1 then,
            Set 'the options stem' to "size={'the size digits'}",
            Set 'the options suffix' to "m".
        If 'the options draw' is 2 then,
            Set 'the options stem' to "mode=0{'the mode digits'}".
        If 'the options draw' is 3 then,
            Set 'the options stem' to "nosuid,nodev,noexec".
        If 'the options draw' is 4 then,
            Set 'the options stem' to "".
        a text called 'the options plain' is "{'the options stem'}{'the options suffix'}",
        a text called 'the options name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "options",
        a list called 'the options parts' is 'gen process mount operand' of 'the options name' and 'the options plain' and 'the options stem' and 'the options suffix',
        a text called 'the options operand' is 'gen process take operand' of 'the options parts' and 'the lines',
        Set 'the mount line' to "{'the mount line'} with options {'the options operand'}".
    a text called 'the flag init' is "a boolean called {'the flag name'} is false".
    a text called 'the handler' is "On error Set {'the flag name'} to true".
    a text called 'the refused assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-14" and 'the flag name'.
    append 'the flag init' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the mount line' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the handler' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the refused assert' to 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the detach flag' is 'gen buffer companion' of "detach refused".
    a text called 'the detach init' is "a boolean called {'the detach flag'} is false".
    a text called 'the detach line' is "Unmount {'the directory name'} lazily".
    a text called 'the detach handler' is "On error Set {'the detach flag'} to true".
    a text called 'the detach assert' is 'gen assert true' of "PRC-21" and 'the detach flag'.
    a text called 'the removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the directory name'.
    append 'the detach init' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the detach line' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the detach handler' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the detach assert' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the removal' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(PRC-15, PRC-16: fstype "none" with options "move" or "bind" is
 recognised and translated into MS_MOVE or MS_BIND
 (LANGUAGE.md:4265-4270). Seen under strace this batch: the literal
 pattern does reach mount(2) as MS_MOVE / MS_BIND with a NULL fstype.
 From inside Vox the translation is not observable - an unprivileged
 mount(2) refuses either way with EPERM - so what this leaf asserts is
 the refusal, and these two rows stay `exercised`. The pattern is only
 ever written as string LITERALS: Discrepancy 8 records that the same
 words held in text variables are NOT translated (they reach the kernel
 as fstype "none", options "bind", no flag), so a variable here would
 put an open discrepancy on trial rather than the documented pattern.
 Each of one or two attempts draws move or bind and whether it moves a
 scratch directory onto itself or onto a second one.)
To 'gen leaf process mount move and bind' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If gen_scratch_flag is empty then,
        Print "PROBE PRC-15: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    a text called 'the first witness' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a list called 'the places' is 'gen process places' of 2.
    a list called 'the names' is [].
    a list called 'the literals' is [].
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 2,
        a text called 'the place' is element 'the position' of 'the places',
        a text called 'the path literal' is "\"{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the place'}{'the path number'}\"",
        a text called 'the path name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "{'the place'}",
        a text called 'the path line' is "a text called {'the path name'} is {'the path literal'}",
        a text called 'the create line' is 'gen process create directory' of 'the path name',
        append 'the path name' to 'the names',
        append 'the path literal' to 'the literals',
        append 'the path line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the create line' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    a number called 'the attempt count' is 'rng below' of 2 add 1.
    Set 'the position' to 1.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the attempt count',
        a number called 'the target slot' is 'rng below' of 2 add 1,
        a text called 'the source variable' is element 1 of 'the names',
        a text called 'the source literal' is element 1 of 'the literals',
        a text called 'the target variable' is element 'the target slot' of 'the names',
        a text called 'the target literal' is element 'the target slot' of 'the literals',
        a text called 'the source operand' is 'gen process path operand' of 'the source variable' and 'the source literal',
        a text called 'the target operand' is 'gen process path operand' of 'the target variable' and 'the target literal',
        a text called 'the ordinal' is 'gen process place spelled' of 'the position',
        a number called 'the move draw' is 'rng below' of 2,
        a text called 'the option' is "bind",
        a text called 'the row' is "PRC-16",
        If 'the move draw' is 1 then,
            Set 'the option' to "move",
            Set 'the row' to "PRC-15".
        a text called 'the flag name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "{'the option'} refused {'the ordinal'}",
        a text called 'the flag init' is "a boolean called {'the flag name'} is false",
        a text called 'the mount line' is "Mount {'the source operand'} at {'the target operand'} with type \"none\" with options \"{'the option'}\"",
        a text called 'the handler' is "On error Set {'the flag name'} to true",
        a text called 'the refused assert' is 'gen assert true' of 'the row' and 'the flag name',
        append 'the flag init' to 'the lines',
        append 'the mount line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the handler' to 'the lines',
        append 'the refused assert' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    Set 'the position' to 2.
    While 'the position' is greater than 0,
        a text called 'the doomed name' is element 'the position' of 'the names',
        a text called 'the removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the doomed name',
        append 'the removal' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' subtract 1.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(An attempt's ordinal as a word, so the flags of two attempts in one
 leaf get distinct names that still read aloud.)
To 'gen process place spelled' with a number called 'the ordinal'.
    If 'the ordinal' is 1 then,
        Return a text, "first".
    If 'the ordinal' is 2 then,
        Return a text, "second".
    If 'the ordinal' is 3 then,
        Return a text, "third".
    Return a text, "fourth".

(PRC-17, PRC-18, PRC-19, PRC-20: `Unmount "<target>".` performs
 umount2(2); `umount` is an accepted alias; a trailing `lazily` requests
 MNT_DETACH (LANGUAGE.md:4271-4275) - all four spellings seen under
 strace this batch reaching umount2(2) with flags 0 or MNT_DETACH. One
 to four attempts, each drawing its verb, whether `lazily` follows, and
 whether it names the target by variable, literal or a buffer copy; the
 target is either a scratch directory the leaf made or a scratch path
 that never existed (the kernel refuses an unprivileged umount2(2) with
 EPERM before it looks the path up, so both are refused). Each refusal
 is asserted under the row its spelling puts on trial; MNT_DETACH's own
 semantics (PRC-20) need a real mount and stay unobservable, so PRC-20
 is `exercised` by the `lazily` spellings.)
To 'gen leaf process unmount spellings' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If gen_scratch_flag is empty then,
        Print "PROBE PRC-17: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    a text called 'the path name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a text called 'the place' is 'gen word from' of gen_process_place_words.
    a text called 'the path literal' is "\"{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the place'}{'the path number'}\"".
    a text called 'the path line' is "a text called {'the path name'} is {'the path literal'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is ['the path line'].
    a number called 'the exists draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the exists draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the create line' is 'gen process create directory' of 'the path name',
        append 'the create line' to 'the lines'.
    a number called 'the copy draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the copy name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "copy".
    If 'the copy draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the copy line' is "a buffer called {'the copy name'} is {'the path name'}",
        append 'the copy line' to 'the lines'.
    a number called 'the attempt count' is 'rng below' of 4 add 1.
    a number called 'the position' is 1.
    While 'the position' is less than or equal to 'the attempt count',
        a number called 'the verb draw' is 'rng below' of 2,
        a number called 'the lazily draw' is 'rng below' of 2,
        a number called 'the operand draw' is 'rng below' of 2 add 'the copy draw',
        a text called 'the verb' is "Unmount",
        a text called 'the row' is "PRC-17",
        If 'the lazily draw' is 1 then,
            Set 'the row' to "PRC-19".
        If 'the verb draw' is 1 then,
            Set 'the verb' to "umount",
            Set 'the row' to "PRC-18".
        a text called 'the operand' is 'the path name',
        If 'the operand draw' is 1 then,
            Set 'the operand' to 'the path literal'.
        If 'the operand draw' is 2 then,
            Set 'the operand' to 'the copy name'.
        a text called 'the statement' is "{'the verb'} {'the operand'}",
        If 'the lazily draw' is 1 then,
            Set 'the statement' to "{'the statement'} lazily".
        a text called 'the ordinal' is 'gen process place spelled' of 'the position',
        a text called 'the flag name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "{'the ordinal'} refusal",
        a text called 'the flag init' is "a boolean called {'the flag name'} is false",
        a text called 'the handler' is "On error Set {'the flag name'} to true",
        a text called 'the refused assert' is 'gen assert true' of 'the row' and 'the flag name',
        append 'the flag init' to 'the lines',
        append 'the statement' to 'the lines',
        append 'the handler' to 'the lines',
        append 'the refused assert' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the position' to 'the position' add 1.
    If 'the exists draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the removal' is 'gen process any removal' of 'the path name',
        append 'the removal' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.

(A device number for the node leaf: any magnitude 'gen extreme number'
 draws, now and then negated. LANGUAGE.md:4286-4287 names `major`/
 `minor` as the standard Linux device numbers and pins no range, and an
 unprivileged mknod(2) is refused before the number means anything -
 so the extremes, which put the encoding on trial, are fair. Note
 Discrepancy 7: a minor above 255 does not survive the encoding.)
To 'gen process device number'.
    a text called 'the digits' is 'gen extreme number'.
    a number called 'the sign draw' is 'rng below' of 5.
    If 'the sign draw' is 0 and 'the digits' is not "0" then,
        Return a text, "-{'the digits'}".
    Return a text, 'the digits'.

(PRC-22, PRC-23, PRC-24: `Create a device node called "<path>" with
 type "c" major N minor M.` performs mknod(2); `type "b"` is accepted;
 the type is "c" or "b" (LANGUAGE.md:4281-4287) - seen under strace this
 batch as mknod(2) with S_IFCHR / S_IFBLK. An unprivileged process lacks
 CAP_MKNOD, so the kernel refuses (EPERM, or EEXIST when the path is
 taken) and the leaf asserts the handler fired. The path is either fresh
 - and then nothing may appear there, which is how a type that lowered
 to anything but a device node (a FIFO needs no privilege and WOULD
 appear, Discrepancy 1) is caught under PRC-24 - or a file the leaf just
 wrote, which must still be there afterwards. Type, path form, and
 whether each number is a literal or a number variable are all drawn.
 Never type "p": see this batch's header.)
To 'gen leaf process device node refusal' with a text called indent and a boolean called nested.
    If gen_does_file_io is false then,
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    If gen_scratch_flag is empty then,
        Print "PROBE PRC-22: gen_does_file_io true but gen_scratch_flag unbound",
        'gen leaf print' of indent,
        Return a boolean, false.
    Set gen_file_ios to gen_file_ios add 1.
    a text called 'the path name' is 'gen process witness'.
    a number called 'the path number' is gen_buffer_names.
    a text called 'the place' is 'gen word from' of gen_process_place_words.
    a text called 'the path plain' is "{{{gen_scratch_flag}}}/{'the place'}{'the path number'}".
    a list called 'the lines' is [].
    a list called 'the path parts' is 'gen process mount operand' of 'the path name' and 'the path plain' and "" and "".
    a text called 'the path operand' is 'gen process take operand' of 'the path parts' and 'the lines'.
    a text called 'the check path' is "\"{'the path plain'}\"".
    a number called 'the occupied draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the handle name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "scribe".
    If 'the occupied draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the open line' is "open a file for writing called {'the handle name'} at {'the check path'}",
        a text called 'the filler' is 'gen buffer filler' of 8,
        a text called 'the write line' is "Write \"{'the filler'}\" to {'the handle name'}",
        a text called 'the close line' is "Close {'the handle name'}",
        append 'the open line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the write line' to 'the lines',
        append 'the close line' to 'the lines'.
    a number called 'the type draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    a text called 'the type' is "c".
    a text called 'the row' is "PRC-22".
    If 'the type draw' is 1 then,
        Set 'the type' to "b",
        Set 'the row' to "PRC-23".
    a text called 'the major' is 'gen process device number'.
    a text called 'the minor' is 'gen process device number'.
    a number called 'the major draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the major draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the major name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "major number",
        a text called 'the major line' is "a number called {'the major name'} is {'the major'}",
        append 'the major line' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the major' to 'the major name'.
    a number called 'the minor draw' is 'rng below' of 2.
    If 'the minor draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the minor name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "minor number",
        a text called 'the minor line' is "a number called {'the minor name'} is {'the minor'}",
        append 'the minor line' to 'the lines',
        Set 'the minor' to 'the minor name'.
    a text called 'the flag name' is 'gen buffer companion' of "node refused".
    a text called 'the flag init' is "a boolean called {'the flag name'} is false".
    a text called 'the node line' is "Create a device node called {'the path operand'} with type \"{'the type'}\" major {'the major'} minor {'the minor'}".
    a text called 'the handler' is "On error Set {'the flag name'} to true".
    a text called 'the refused assert' is 'gen assert true' of 'the row' and 'the flag name'.
    append 'the flag init' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the node line' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the handler' to 'the lines'.
    append 'the refused assert' to 'the lines'.
    If 'the occupied draw' is 0 then,
        a text called 'the absent assert' is 'gen process assert absent' of "PRC-24" and 'the check path' and "no node appeared",
        append 'the absent assert' to 'the lines'.
    If 'the occupied draw' is 1 then,
        a text called 'the present assert' is 'gen process assert present' of 'the row' and 'the check path' and "the file is still there",
        a text called 'the cleanup' is "Delete the file {'the check path'}",
        append 'the present assert' to 'the lines',
        append 'the cleanup' to 'the lines'.
    'gen join lines' of indent and nested and 'the lines'.
